    "created_at": "2024-07-15T14:16:16Z",
    "updated_at": "2024-07-15T14:16:16Z",
    "body": "They'd both get attributed to the event handler as the JS stack will be non-empty by the time you get to the promise though.\r\n\r\nI think it also gets confusing if you resolve multiple promises in a single task.\r\n\r\nI don't like using \"resolve\" and \"reject\" as entry points coupled with the JS stack being empty as in my mind that's very much against the way promises are designed. Tying this directly to tasks (that may execute script) seems much more natural.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
